<title>FRANCE: Legrand buys India MDS fuse maker.</title>
<headline>Legrand buys India MDS fuse maker.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>French electrical company Legrand said on Friday it had bought India's MDS which makes electrical fuses.</p>
<p>MDS has factories in the Bombay area and has turnover of 60 million francs and a &quot;good level of profitability,&quot; Legrand said in a statement.</p>
<p>The acquisition would allow the French firm to take a position in a market with &quot;considerable potential&quot; and demonstrated its wish to expand internationally, especially in emerging markets, it said.</p>
<p>It gave no purchase details.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 pnt</p>
